index 0000000..cc9681d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Single-server deployment
+
+This deployment runs Fizzy on one Linux server with Docker. SQLite and local
+Active Storage data live in a named Docker volume, while Solid Queue runs in
+Puma inside the application container. Kamal's proxy terminates HTTPS.
+
+## Before setup
+
+1. Point a DNS hostname at the server.
+2. Open ports 22, 80, and 443 on the server.
+3. Install Docker and enable SSH access for the deployment user.
+4. Create a GitHub Container Registry (GHCR) package or change the registry to
+   the container registry you use.
+
+## Configure Kamal
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+* Set `image` to your registry image name.
+* Set `servers.web.hosts` to the server hostname or IP address.
+* Set `proxy.host` to the public DNS hostname.
+* Set `APP_HOST`, `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`,
+  `SMTP_DOMAIN`, and `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION` for your mail provider.
+
+Edit `.kamal/secrets` if you use a secrets manager. The default file expects
+these values in the shell environment:
+
+* `KAMAL_REGISTRY_USERNAME` and `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`
+* `RAILS_MASTER_KEY` and `SECRET_KEY_BASE`
+* `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD`
+* `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+
+Generate independent application secrets and export them before deployment:
+
+```sh
+export RAILS_MASTER_KEY="$(ruby -rsecurerandom -e 'print SecureRandom.hex(16)')"
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE="$(ruby -rsecurerandom -e 'print SecureRandom.hex(64)')"
+export KAMAL_REGISTRY_USERNAME="your-github-username"
+export KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD="your-ghcr-token"
+export SMTP_USERNAME="your-smtp-username"
+export SMTP_PASSWORD="your-smtp-password"
+```
+
+The VAPID values are only needed for web push. Leave them unset if you do not
+use that feature.
+
+The SSH user defaults to the local user. Set `ssh.user` in `config/deploy.yml`
+if the server uses a different deployment account.
+
+## Deploy
+
+Run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Later deploys use:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+The `fizzy-storage:/rails/storage` named volume contains the SQLite databases
+and uploaded files. It remains attached across app container replacements and
+redeployments. The normal backup policy for your server should include that
+Docker volume.
